Case 01 — Solar Open 2 x Claude Code — solar-pro4 local verification
Date: 2026-08-03
Model: solar-pro4 (via docker/litellm-proxy, use_chat_completions_url_for_anthropic_messages=true)

Upstage's own Anthropic-compatible endpoint has no model mapping for
solar-pro4 (see 01-solar-open2-harness Method B against
https://api.upstage.ai directly: no response). This proxy exists to
close that gap for any Anthropic-format client.

== Raw request, identical wire format to what Claude Code sends ==

$ curl "http://127.0.0.1:4000/v1/messages?beta=true" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-local-solar-proxy" \
    -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"model":"solar-pro4","max_tokens":16,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}'

{"id":"a93a14f4-f110-48a0-8c8e-bb4d4356ef6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"solar-pro4", ...
"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, the user just said \"hi\". That's a simple greeting. I"...}],
"stop_reason":"max_tokens"}

RESULT: PASS — solar-pro4 answers correctly through the Anthropic-shaped
/v1/messages bridge, same as solar-open2.

== Note: direct `claude -p "hello"` CLI invocation ==

Running the bare `claude` binary as a subprocess from *this* development
session (itself a Claude Code Desktop host) failed with:

  API Error: 400 No connected db.

Root cause (confirmed via proxy logs + `env | grep -i claude`): this
session's own ambient environment carries CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_SCOPES /
CLAUDE_CODE_SDK_HAS_OAUTH_REFRESH, which the spawned `claude` CLI
subprocess inherits and prioritizes over the exported
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, so it authenticates to the local proxy with the
host session's own token instead of the proxy's master key — which the
proxy (no database configured) can't validate as a virtual key. This is
an artifact of testing `claude` nested inside a Claude Code session, not
a defect in the proxy or in solar-pro4 support. Confirmed absent when
invoked via the Claude Agent SDK instead (see case-03-solar-pro4.log),
which builds a clean subprocess environment.

VERDICT: solar-pro4 works through the litellm-proxy bridge for
Anthropic-format Claude Code traffic (raw wire-format + SDK-mediated CLI
both confirmed). The bare-CLI failure is a local, nested-session
credential-precedence artifact specific to this dev environment.
